{
    "background_story": "Maya was a Haast's eagle, a prehistoric bird of prey that ruled the skies of New Zealand during the Pleistocene era. Also known as Haastia, this majestic creature was the largest eagle to have ever existed. Maya was a skilled hunter, using her sharp talons and powerful beak to take down prey much larger than herself. She soared through the forests and mountains, her wings beating effortlessly as she scanned the ground below for her next meal. With her exceptional eyesight and agility, Maya was a formidable hunter, earning the respect and fear of the other creatures in her domain. Her domain was one of rugged beauty, and Maya was its undisputed queen, reigning supreme over the ancient landscape.",
